  "rules": [
    "Every relationship is directional; A's trust in B is not copied to B.",
    "Family creates opportunity for contact and obligation, not automatic affection.",
    "Friendship likelihood depends on proximity, repeated contact, age, value similarity and extraversion.",
    "Rivalry requires repeated contact or shared status competition; it is never random between strangers.",
    "Cross-settlement ties arise through transport, trade, migration-like household history or specialized work.",
    "No cross-country social edge exists before first contact.",
    "Every adult must have at least two meaningful nonzero social ties; every minor must have a caregiver/family tie.",
    "No citizen is retroactively invented to create a network role."
